/* book exam traps: Thinking boundary scan tests the logic inside the chip. It tests pins and board wiring; the core needs scan or BIST. | Using one chip's IR length for the board. In a daisy chain the instruction lengths add, and so do the selected data-register lengths. | Forgetting that the last shift happens on the edge that leaves Shift-DR: n bits need n edges in the Shift state, the last with TMS = 1. | Saying SAMPLE/PRELOAD drives the board. It only captures pin values and preloads the cells; EXTEST drives. | Treating TMS as a data pin. TDI and TDO carry data, TMS steers the state machine, TCK clocks both. */
