/* book exam traps: Counting 2ⁿ states for a maximal-length LFSR. The period is 2ⁿ − 1; the all-zero word never appears. | Seeding with all zeros. The register locks up at 000…0 and makes no vectors. | Reading a BIST pass as proof of a good chip. A faulty circuit can alias to the golden signature. | Expecting a MISR to say which output was wrong. It only compresses; diagnosis needs the raw responses. | Saying BIST makes ATPG unnecessary. Random-pattern-resistant faults still need weighted, reseeded or ATPG vectors, checked by fault simulation. */
